       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO TID, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as no more than 850 mg per dose. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** The ordered dose is twice the maximum daily dose. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1,700 mg/day total, for example 850 mg PO BID with meals\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO BID with meals\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and whether it's immediate-release or extended-release. I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg TID, please confirm that explicitly. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
